  "worked_solution": "Since the number of computers in the data center obeys an inhibited growth model, the rate at which the number of computers changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the number of computers in the data center. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-C),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity of the data center, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=1000$ computers, and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(1000-C).\n$$",
